# Resolution
Fixed by commit b6c176a6 (`Continue phase 11 runtime map refresh`). The frontend startup path now wraps the bootstrap `StorageCluster` in `StorageClusterRuntimeMapHandle`, starts a frontend control-plane runtime-map refresh loop when `ARGMIN_CONTROL_PLANE_SOCKET_PATH` is configured, and constructs frontend coordinators from the shared handle rather than from immutable one-shot `Arc<StorageCluster>` clones. The refresh loop preserves configured Unix storage-node RPC admission settings and updates the handle as control-plane runtime maps advance.

Additional regression coverage was added in `remote_frontend_control_plane_refresh_loop_updates_bootstrap_map`: the test bootstraps a dynamic frontend from a peering control-plane runtime map, then serves an active map to the frontend refresh loop and verifies that the same frontend runtime-map handle advances to `PgState::Active`. This pins the `argmin-s3` boundary that was missing in the original vulnerable commit.

# Summary
Introduced an availability regression for control-plane-routed frontends. Static frontend routing is unaffected, but the newly enabled dynamic frontend path can become unusable after the initial heartbeat lease window, which defaults to 1000 ms and is capped at 10000 ms.
The commit lets frontend/combined roles omit static ARGMIN_STORAGE_NODE_SOCKETS when ARGMIN_CONTROL_PLANE_SOCKET_PATH is set, and builds the frontend StorageCluster from a one-time control-plane runtime map snapshot. That runtime map includes valid_until_ms derived from primary lease deadlines. The resulting StorageCluster is then cloned directly into immutable Coordinator instances, with no StorageClusterRuntimeMapHandle or refresh loop retained for the frontend. Once the initial valid_until_ms is reached, LocalClusterMap rejects metadata routing and payload placement with RouteMapExpired, so normal S3 operations through a dynamic frontend fail until the process is restarted or otherwise rebuilt. Storage nodes get a refresh loop in this commit, but frontends do not.

