## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the commit enables the affected deployment mode: frontend/combined roles can use ARGMIN_CONTROL_PLANE_SOCKET_PATH without static ARGMIN_STORAGE_NODE_SOCKETS.
- [x] Confirm the dynamic frontend path fetches a single control-plane runtime-map snapshot and constructs StorageCluster from it.
- [x] Confirm control-plane runtime maps for Active PGs include finite valid_until_ms derived from primary lease deadlines.
- [x] Confirm the StorageCluster/LocalClusterMap rejects use after valid_until_ms with RouteMapExpired.
- [x] Confirm frontend startup does not retain StorageClusterRuntimeMapHandle or spawn a refresh loop, while storage-node control-plane startup does.
## Report
Validated the availability regression. I added a targeted PoC unit test to argmin-s3 that exercises the actual dynamic frontend startup path: it serves one active control-plane runtime-map snapshot over a Unix socket, calls build_remote_frontend_storage_cluster(), waits past the snapshot lease deadline, then checks the resulting frontend StorageCluster. The reproduction command `cargo test -p argmin-s3 remote_frontend_control_plane_cluster_expires_without_refresh -- --nocapture` passed while printing: `frontend one-shot runtime map valid_until_ms=1781603863571, now_ms=1781603863442` and then `after initial lease window frontend cluster returns: runtime route map for cluster epoch 5 expired at 1781603863571; current time is 1781603863597`. This confirms the dynamic frontend cluster becomes expired after the initial lease window. I also ran an existing storage-layer test, `cargo test -p storage runtime_map_builds_storage_cluster_with_validity_bound -- --nocapture`, which passed and asserts that StorageCluster::from_runtime_map carries valid_until_ms and returns StoreError::RouteMapExpired at the deadline. Debugger evidence: lldb breakpoint at `argmin_s3::build_control_plane_frontend_storage_cluster` stopped at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:759, called from `build_remote_frontend_storage_cluster` at main.rs:722; a second breakpoint stopped at `storage::cluster::local::LocalClusterMap::require_route_map_valid_at` at crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:1579, called from `StorageCluster::require_route_map_valid_at` at crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:2285 with now_ms greater than the printed valid_until_ms. Code evidence matches the suspected finding: config permits frontend/combined roles to omit static sockets when a control-plane socket exists at crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:316-320; dynamic frontend startup fetches exactly one UnixControlPlaneClient runtime-map snapshot and builds a StorageCluster from it at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:721-784; frontend coordinators receive only cloned Arc<StorageCluster> values at main.rs:820-842, with no StorageClusterRuntimeMapHandle or refresh loop retained; storage-node startup does have a control-plane refresh loop at main.rs:546-578. The runtime map is lease-bounded because ClusterControlSnapshot::runtime_map sets valid_until_ms from the minimum primary lease deadline at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:388-395, and LocalClusterMap rejects expired maps with StoreError::RouteMapExpired at crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:1578-1582. Crash/valgrind/ASan attempts: this is not a memory-safety crash bug, so the direct PoC did not crash but reproduced the availability failure. `valgrind --version` failed with command not found. `RUSTFLAGS='-Z sanitizer=address' cargo test ... --no-run` failed because the stable compiler rejects `-Z sanitizer=address` without nightly.

